## Enhancement Guide

The validation system can be enhanced with these features:

### 1. Summary Reports

Add summary statistics at the end of validation:

```powershell
function Generate-ValidationSummary {
    param (
        [hashtable]$ValidationResults
    )
    
    $totalFiles = $ValidationResults.FilesChecked
    $errorCount = $ValidationResults.Errors.Count
    $warningCount = $ValidationResults.Warnings.Count
    $cleanFiles = $totalFiles - ($ValidationResults.FilesWithIssues.Count)
    $cleanPercentage = [math]::Round(($cleanFiles / $totalFiles) * 100, 1)
    
    Write-Host "Validation Summary:"
    Write-Host "- Files checked: $totalFiles"
    Write-Host "- Errors found: $errorCount"
    Write-Host "- Warnings found: $warningCount"
    Write-Host "- Clean files: $cleanFiles ($cleanPercentage%)"
}
```

### 2. Export Options

Add ability to export results to CSV or JSON:

```powershell
function Export-ValidationResults {
    param (
        [hashtable]$ValidationResults,
        [string]$ExportPath,
        [string]$Format = "CSV"
    )
    
    $exportData = @()
    
    foreach ($error in $ValidationResults.Errors) {
        $exportData += [PSCustomObject]@{
            Type = "Error"
            File = $error.File
            Issue = $error.Issue
            Line = $error.Line
            Fix = $error.Fix
        }
    }
    
    foreach ($warning in $ValidationResults.Warnings) {
        $exportData += [PSCustomObject]@{
            Type = "Warning"
            File = $warning.File
            Issue = $warning.Issue
            Line = $warning.Line
            Fix = $warning.Fix
        }
    }
    
    if ($Format -eq "CSV") {
        $exportData | Export-Csv -Path $ExportPath -NoTypeInformation
    } elseif ($Format -eq "JSON") {
        $exportData | ConvertTo-Json | Out-File -FilePath $ExportPath
    }
}
```

### 3. Filter Capabilities

Add filters for specific directories or file types:

```powershell
function Get-ValidationTargets {
    param (
        [string]$RootPath,
        [string[]]$IncludeDirectories,
        [string[]]$ExcludeDirectories,
        [string[]]$FileTypes = @("*.md")
    )
    
    $targets = @()
    
    # Build include pattern
    $includePattern = if ($IncludeDirectories) {
        $IncludeDirectories | ForEach-Object { [regex]::Escape($_) } | Join-String -Separator "|"
    } else {
        ".*"
    }
    
    # Build exclude pattern
    $excludePattern = if ($ExcludeDirectories) {
        $ExcludeDirectories | ForEach-Object { [regex]::Escape($_) } | Join-String -Separator "|"
    } else {
        "^$" # Match nothing
    }
    
    # Get all files matching the patterns
    foreach ($fileType in $FileTypes) {
        $files = Get-ChildItem -Path $RootPath -Filter $fileType -Recurse |
                Where-Object {
                    $_.FullName -match $includePattern -and
                    $_.FullName -notmatch $excludePattern
                }
        $targets += $files
    }
    
    return $targets
}
```

